id: pm-bw8lsb
title: Explain rejected telemetry source-context overrides without leaking raw values
description: "GitHub source https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1253. GitHub reports that unrecognized PM_TELEMETRY_SOURCE_CONTEXT values silently fall back to inferred automation and contaminate attribution. Existing accepted contexts and hard opt-outs must remain stable; rejected values may contain private data and must not be copied verbatim into events."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-12T22:29:57.940Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T22:29:57.940Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Accepted absent and rejected overrides have distinct tested behavior; rejection produces a bounded diagnostic naming accepted values; emitted attribution exposes rejection through a fixed marker without raw custom values; hard opt-outs still suppress all capture.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Explain rejected telemetry source-context overrides without leaking raw values
value: Lower agent recovery cost and preserve safe customizable SDK composition
parent: pm-5oj5
